---
const readme = 'https://github.com/Shimodos/Backdrop#which-image-belongs-to-the-scene';

const ways = [
  {
    title: 'Without Scene Manager',
    lead: 'Plain 3ds Max: cameras, and Batch Render if you use it.',
    blocks: [
      {
        label: 'Set up once',
        text: 'Name each camera like its image, or keep a Batch Render view per camera whose output file is named like the image.',
      },
      {
        label: 'The image follows the camera',
        text: 'Look through another camera and its image comes up with its comments. The status line says what the image was found by, and lists the names it tried when nothing fits.',
      },
      {
        label: 'A click goes to the camera',
        text: 'Click a preview and the camera of that image is put in the viewport.',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'With Pulze Scene Manager 2',
    lead: 'Nothing to set up: the setups are already named like their images.',
    blocks: [
      {
        label: 'The image follows the setup',
        text: 'Activate a setup in Scene Manager and its image comes up: the panel reads the name from the render output Scene Manager writes.',
      },
      {
        label: 'A click goes to the setup',
        text: 'Click a preview and the panel takes the camera, the frame, the shown and hidden layers, the render output file and the resolution of the setup named like that image.',
      },
      {
        label: 'Same camera, other layers',
        text: 'Two setups on one camera and one frame that differ only in layers are told apart: the click switches the layers.',
      },
    ],
  },
];

const notes = [
  ['Save the scene after changing setups.', 'The panel reads them from the scene file as it was last saved.'],
  ['Scene Manager does not know about the click.', 'Its own list stays on the setup chosen there, and a render started from Scene Manager uses that one.'],
  ['Close the Render Setup dialog before clicking.', '3ds Max may not keep an output file and a resolution set from a script while it is open.'],
];
---

<section id="shots" class="border-t border-line bg-card dark:border-line-dark dark:bg-card-dark">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-24">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-accent-deep uppercase dark:text-accent">Image and shot</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl">The image follows the scene, and the scene follows a click</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-muted text-pretty dark:text-ink-muted-dark">
        An image and a shot are tied by name. Change the shot and its image comes up; click an image and the
        scene goes to its shot. What a shot is depends on how the scene is built, and both ways work in the
        same panel with nothing to switch.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid items-start gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      {ways.map((way) => (
        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-paper p-7 ring-1 ring-line dark:bg-paper-dark dark:ring-line-dark">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">{way.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-[15px] text-ink-muted dark:text-ink-muted-dark">{way.lead}</p>
          <dl class="mt-6 space-y-5">
            {way.blocks.map((block, i) => (
              <div class="flex gap-3">
                <span class="mt-0.5 grid size-5 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-xs font-semibold text-accent-deep dark:bg-accent/15 dark:text-accent">{i + 1}</span>
                <div>
                  <dt class="font-medium">{block.label}</dt>
                  <dd class="mt-1 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted dark:text-ink-muted-dark">{block.text}</dd>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-paper p-7 ring-1 ring-line dark:bg-paper-dark dark:ring-line-dark">
      <h3 class="font-semibold tracking-tight">With Scene Manager, three things to know</h3>
      <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-5 text-[15px] leading-relaxed md:grid-cols-3">
        {notes.map(([head, text]) => (
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">{head}</span>
            <span class="text-ink-muted dark:text-ink-muted-dark"> {text}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[15px] text-ink-muted dark:text-ink-muted-dark">
        Names are compared loosely: case, spaces and separators do not matter, and a suffix on either side is
        allowed.
        <a href={readme} class="font-medium text-accent-deep underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-4 transition hover:decoration-accent dark:text-accent">The full rules are in the README.</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
